WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.640
I think I can, I think I can, I think I can.

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:12.800
And over the mountain the little engine went.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:16.119
We’re going to get over that mountain, I
have no doubt about it.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:20.520
Gov. Jerry Brown championed a high speed rail
that would connect southern and Northern California,

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:25.620
despite cost overruns, lawsuits over land
use, and a lack of private investment.

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:29.820
Now, that high speed rail plan is being scaled
back by new governor, Gavin Newsom.

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:36.059
The current project as planneds would cost
too much and respectfully take too long.

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:39.120
What Gavin Newsom has done is he’s spit
in Jerry Brown’s eye.

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:42.260
Newsom basically said, Jerry this is your
little choo-choo

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:45.260
and I can’t afford to pay for your dream.

00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:47.840
Columnist and fellow at Chapman University
Joel Kotkin

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:50.660
has been skeptical of California’s high
speed rail for years

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:52.539
and says that the only reason Brown stuck
with it

00:00:52.539 --> 00:00:55.859
was because it offered him a chance to have
some sort of physical legacy.

00:00:55.859 --> 00:01:00.970
Jerry Brown was the only reason why this thing
hadn’t been killed before.

00:01:00.970 --> 00:01:03.760
Gavin Newsom is looking at the future and
saying,

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:05.860
you know, we're going to have all sorts of
fiscal issues,

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:08.860
they're all things we want to do and this
is an absurdity.

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:12.760
The high speed rail will now only stretch
to Bakersfield to Merced.

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:16.220
And that’s not going to be easy because
there is just not a lot of money to be made

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:18.080
between Bakersfield and Merced.

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:20.100
This is the ultimate train to nowhere,

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:24.740
going from two places that, don't have any
particular relationship with each other.

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:28.180
It's a part of the, of the state where people
actually drive.

00:01:28.189 --> 00:01:30.490
The vast majority of people drive.

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:33.020
By the time got the station you still have
to drive.

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:38.680
It's not like going from a place where people
live because they can afford to, to a job center.

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:40.840
There's no job center involved here.

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:43.100
And here's the thing that really bothers me:

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:46.630
The Central Valley has very serious economic
problems.

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:50.400
There is huge degrees of poverty, unemployment,

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:54.360
some of the poorest parts of the United States
are in the central valley.

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:57.840
And we're doing this kind of fancy choo choo?

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:01.380
He says the high speed rail was always a solution
in search of a problem.

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:09.380
The problems in California are not getting
from LA or Orange County to San Jose or San Francisco.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:11.900
Southwest does a spectacularly good job.

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:14.740
We have all these regional airports.

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:20.560
Most people in the major population centers
are 15, 20 minutes,

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:27.520
maybe a half hour away from an airport where
they can go in an hour directly to where they want to go.

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:30.600
The problems in California are inside the
state.

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:34.130
It's getting from one part of southern California
to another.

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:37.020
It's a problem of getting from one part of
the Bay area to another.

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:38.780
And this didn't address that at all.

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:44.540
Everything from the Great Society to the New
Deal started with a vision for our future.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:47.760
Green New Deal backers say they want more
high speed trains.

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:51.140
As a place to replace air travel and add green
jobs.

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:54.700
This is a shot across the bow for the green
new deal.

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:58.870
The green new deal is, is based on, you know,
some ideas of people

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:03.460
that you ever wonder if they ever actually
realized how big the United States is.

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:08.140
You know, when people say, we could be just
like Europe, well Europe is much smaller.

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:10.750
The distances between cities has, are much
less.

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:15.420
The cities were built, in many cases, two,
three, 400 years ago, sometimes more.

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:19.020
And they were built around trains to start
with.

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:22.580
Even so 80% of the people in Europe drive
to work.

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:28.370
So the, the idea that you would go to a country
where 90, 95% of the people drive to work

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:30.790
and that you are going to replace the roads

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:35.590
or that most of the long distance travel,
the vast majority of it takes place in airplanes

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:36.900
is just lunacy.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:39.910
I think that some of these people, like
AOC,

00:03:39.910 --> 00:03:44.400
I think somebody ought to, you know, put them
in a car and say let's drive to Nebraska

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:49.760
and let's see how practical a train would
be to get to Omaha.

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:51.320
It's not very practical at all.

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:52.840
So what’s Newsom doing here?

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:54.450
He’s basically scaling back.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:59.720
He’s buying time to try and save money and
hopefully get more money to get it going again.

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:03.900
The real battle in the Democratic Party is
between reality and fantasy.

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:06.280
And this was a big win for reality.

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:10.400
People knew this was an incredibly stupid
boondoggle.

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:13.060
And of course what’s really going to be
interesting is:

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:15.660
Is any other state going to be as stupid as
we are?

